WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
- You're spearheading
actually something called

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.690
the #NotAlone Challenge.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.079
So tell us about that.

00:00:05.079 --> 00:00:07.410
- Yeah, so I moved out at 15.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.180
I knew statistically, kids like me

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.350
end up repeating the cycle

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.940
and I didn't wanna be a statistic.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.060
I grew up in a family where
abuse had been generational

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.529
and so, I wanted to see if
happiness was a learnable skill.

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:19.980
So, I learned a lot of skills for myself

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.510
that really helped me learn

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.580
what I call a new emotional language,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.560
because not everybody
has access to therapy.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.260
In fact, 50% of the people
that need mental health help

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.120
don't have access to any tools.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.530
And happiness shouldn't be elite.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.700
It shouldn't be just for the people

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.580
that can afford something
or afford a therapist.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.360
So the #NotAlone Challenge
is bringing proven tools

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.040
that can scale to everybody

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.140
that lives in these mental health deserts.

00:00:44.196 --> 00:00:45.960
- I love, that is so important.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.010
And it's also like, not only
that people can't afford it.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.940
I know people like from
where I'm from in the South,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.830
it's still kind of looked down upon

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.470
and people get shamed for it,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.388
which is such a crazy thing to me,

00:01:00.388 --> 00:01:03.060
for lack of a better word,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.310
because it's one of those things

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.010
it's nice to have somebody
outside your circle

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.560
that literally is trained in
ways to help you navigate,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.920
give you tools with whatever
you're dealing with.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.620
It's like if you need help with your car,

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.450
you go to a mechanic, if you need help,

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.530
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.300
It just seems so natural to me,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.330
but it's not only, it's
amazing 'cause the money

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.510
but also, I think society
needs to really change

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:31.170
and evolve in the sense of
quit shaming people for it

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.150
or looking down upon it.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:33.983
- Yeah.

00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:35.640
- But how could people get involved?

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.810
- Oh, if you wanna get involved,

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.420
go to NotAlonechallenge.org

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.030
and there you'll find a lot of
mental health tools for free.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.860
You'll find a ton of resources

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.560
and then you can also find all
of our auction items there.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.240
And we have incredible auction items.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.560
We're raising money to be able

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.570
to scale proven behavioral tools

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.638
so that everybody has access to them.

00:01:53.638 --> 00:01:55.050
(audience clapping)

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.393
- That's incredible,
Jewel, that's so cool.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.990
So I hear that there's an auction

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.760
and even like tickets,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.490
from sports tickets to
like Billy Eilish tickets.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.860
You're offering something
cool as well, right?

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.350
- Yeah, I thought that I would
write a personalized song

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.540
so people can bid on a
song that I'll write.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.500
I'll write about your dog

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.850
if that's what you want
me to write it about.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.570
I'll write about your mama,
I'll write about your son.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:22.050
But I thought that'd be fun
so people can bid on that.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.520
- I love, that's such a cool thing.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.010
It's such a personal
thing to do for someone.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.093
It's really cool.

